# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Minecraft Paper server — .gitignore
#
# Principle: version the things you AUTHOR (source, scripts, docs).
# Ignore everything the server GENERATES or DOWNLOADS — all of it is
# reproducible from a fresh run, and most of it is large, churning,
# or contains secrets and player data.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Server binaries ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The Paper jar is ~59 MB. GitHub warns above 50 MB and hard-rejects
# 100 MB, and it's a signed public download — re-fetch it instead.
# See the README for the exact build and its checksum.
paper-*.jar

# Compiled Java artifacts generally (your plugin jars included —
# build them, don't commit them).
*.jar
*.class
# ...except the Gradle wrapper jar, which IS meant to be committed
# so anyone cloning can build without installing Gradle first.
# The **/ prefix matters: a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the repo
# root, so plain `gradle/wrapper/...` would miss sample-plugins/gradle/wrapper/.
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar

# ── Paper's downloaded/patched runtime (~165 MB) ─────────────
# Regenerated automatically on first run: Paper fetches Mojang's
# vanilla jar and applies its patches.
cache/
libraries/
versions/
.paper/

# ── Secrets and configuration ────────────────────────────────
# server.properties holds generated credentials:
#   management-server-secret   (auto-generated, live value)
#   rcon.password              (if you ever enable RCON)
# Never commit it. See the README for how to share settings safely.
server.properties

# ── World data ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The live world changes every single tick and merges catastrophically, so it stays
# out of git. The archived realms are finished history and ARE tracked — see below.
world/
world_nether/
world_the_end/

# Staging folders for importing an old save. `/mv import` consumes these, so they
# exist only between the copy and the import — but never let one get committed.
#
# These need the leading slash. Without it, `old/` matches a directory named `old`
# at ANY depth, which would silently re-ignore the archived realm below.
/old/
/oldest/
/oldest_nether/
/oldest_the_end/

# ── current/ — the default world, and every other world too ──
# On Paper 26.2 a world is a dimension inside the default world's folder, so
# current/ holds all seven. Ignore it wholesale, then re-include the finished
# realms so a fresh clone still has them.
#
# Each level is unignored on the way down rather than with one `current/` line,
# because git will not re-include a path inside an already-excluded directory.
current/*
!current/dimensions/
current/dimensions/*
!current/dimensions/minecraft/
current/dimensions/minecraft/*

# The archived realms — tracked. `current`'s own overworld/nether/end are not.
!current/dimensions/minecraft/old/
!current/dimensions/minecraft/oldest/
!current/dimensions/minecraft/oldest_nether/
!current/dimensions/minecraft/oldest_the_end/

*/session.lock

# ── Backups ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# World archives are large and binary. Keep the folder, never the contents.
backups/*
!backups/.gitkeep

# ── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs/
*.log
*.log.gz
crash-reports/
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# ── Player and moderation data ───────────────────────────────
# Contains usernames, UUIDs, and IP addresses.
ops.json
whitelist.json
banned-players.json
banned-ips.json
usercache.json
permissions.yml
help.yml

# ── Plugin runtime state ─────────────────────────────────────
# Config and data directories plugins create for themselves.
# Keep the folder itself so a fresh clone has somewhere to drop jars.
plugins/*
!plugins/.gitkeep

# ── Generated server configs ─────────────────────────────────
# Regenerated with sane defaults on first boot. Uncomment any you
# deliberately tune and want tracked — but check for secrets first.
bukkit.yml
spigot.yml
commands.yml
config/

# ── EULA ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accepting Minecraft's EULA is a personal legal act. Let whoever
# runs the server accept it themselves rather than inheriting yours.
eula.txt

# ── Plugin build output (Gradle / Maven) ─────────────────────
build/
.gradle/
gradle-app.setting
target/
out/
bin/
!src/**/bin/

# ── IDEs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project
*.code-workspace

# ── OS cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Editors / misc ───────────────────────────────────────────
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.env
.env.local
